  "_sourceRefs": [
    "PyX12 (azoner/pyx12) 837.5010.X222.A1.xml — the ENTIRE 2300 subtree (2310A-F, 2320->2330A-G, 2400->2410/2420A-H/2430/2440) appears in TWO tree positions within 837P: under 2000B (subscriber is the patient) and under 2000C (a dependent is the patient) — confirmed via line-count comparison of both real occurrences (~11,371 vs ~11,379 lines, same shape, not two different structures that happen to share a loop ID). Authored ONCE here per the Phase 2 loopRef mechanism (edi/schema_disk_types... see edi/schema_loader.go's resolveLoopRefs) and referenced from both 837P.json's and 837I.json's own 2000B/2000C positions via {\"loopRef\": \"2300-claim\"} — see CLAUDE.md's EDI Phase 2 section for the full design rationale.",
    "TRIGGER DISCRIMINATORS added (September 2026, found via real-sample 837-to-FHIR-mapping testing): 2310A-F all share the bare 'NM1' trigger, and matchLoops' own schema-order-only matching silently mis-assigned a token to whichever earlier-declared sibling hadn't been consumed yet whenever a real claim's providers didn't appear in the exact 2310A/B/C/D/E/F order (routine — most real professional claims populate only a subset, e.g. Rendering + Service Facility with nothing else). NM1-01 (Entity Identifier Code) values are well-established, long-standing X12 healthcare codes: DN=Referring Provider, 82=Rendering Provider, 77=Service Facility Location, DQ=Supervising Provider, PW=Ambulance Pick-up Location, 45=Ambulance Drop-off Location."
  ]
